    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup today is headlined by two elite plays: **Kyle Tucker** (77.96) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.27). **Tucker** benefits from a high-floor matchup against McCullers Jr., where his base projection is bolstered by an 18% boost due to the favorable SP matchup. Meanwhile, **Merrill** secures a top-tier score thanks to his leadoff spot and a strong platoon advantage, though we are tempering expectations slightly regarding his base-stealing potential given the 1.86s pop time of the opposing catcher. **Gunnar Henderson** (73.50) remains a cornerstone of our offensive strategy today; his ability to exploit a slow-delivering pitcher against P\u00e9rez, Eu, paired with his leadoff positioning, makes him a primary engine for our category production, particularly in R and SB.\n\nOn the bench, **Nolan Schanuel** (55.01) was the most difficult exclusion, narrowly missing the cut behind the dynamic speed threat of **Nasim Nunez** and the platoon-advantaged **Sam Antonacci**. While **Schanuel** possesses a solid matchup profile against the left-handed Schultz, our optimizer prioritized the higher efficiency ceiling provided by **Antonacci** (67.67), whose xwOBA of .407 and favorable placement against Ure\u00f1a make him a critical asset for our daily efficiency targets. We are also monitoring the status of **Marcell Ozuna**; despite a decent score of 49.52, the combination of his \"Lineup Pending\" status and lower raw projection relative to our starting outfielders kept him on the bench. \n\nInvestors should note the elevated risk profiles for both **Jacob Wilson** and **Josh Jung**. **Wilson** faces the elite arm of Wheeler, which severely hampers his projection despite the benefit of a favorable wind; we are starting him, but his 47.63 score reflects that difficulty. Conversely, **Josh Jung** is being held in reserve not just for performance reasons, but due to a 45% rain risk at his venue. We are confident in today's alignment to maximize our 5x5 output while maintaining our strict adherence to efficiency thresholds.",
